@doc """
Standard `Decode` trait declaration.
`Decode<$To>` converts `Self` into `$To`.
The `to` parameter is a signature-level TypeRef witness slot and is not meant
to be observed at runtime.
Format-specific value owners such as `JsonValue` expose their own helper
surface, for example `JsonValue::decode(value, Target)`.

## REPL
xldr(1)> json =? Json::decode("{\"name\":\"surtr\"}")
xldr(2)> JsonValue::decode(json, String)
Ok(Object(hash!["name" => String("surtr")]))
"""
deftrait Decode<$To> {
  # Convert the value into the requested target type.
  def decode(self: Self, to: TypeRef<$To>) -> Result<$To, Error>
}
